context_info = ""
for d in context:
    result = llm_query("You are given one document. Determine if it contains or implies the same series as described by the following plot points. If it does, extract the series name and match the plot points with evidence (season/Episode mentions, character names). If it does not, just say it does not match.\n\nTarget plot points to match:\n1) Early in Season 1: after a tense moment when one lead assumes they won't be spending time together due to a sensitive/sensitive-topic issue, the other gets upset. Friends convince the first person to take their partner out on a date to make things right.\n2) One of the final episodes of Season 3: the male lead's roommate makes a sacrifice.\n3) Midway through Season 4: the female lead returns home for the birth of a family member's baby, but instead of focusing on the event, she unexpectedly reconnects with someone from the past.\nConstraint: The show has fewer than 10 seasons.\n\nFor this single document, output in this format:\n- Match: Yes/No/Unclear\n- Candidate series name(s): ...\n- Evidence (quotes with season/episode if present) mapping to each plot point 1, 2, 3.\n- Notes: any helpful disambiguation clues (character names, locations, network, year).\n\nBEGIN_DOCUMENT\n" + d + "\nEND_DOCUMENT")
    context_info = context_info + "\n\n=== Document Analysis ===\n" + result

final_answer = llm_query("You are deciding the single best series that fits the user's three plot points, using only the summarized document analyses below. Prefer candidates where all three plot points are clearly evidenced (season/episode and character names) and the series has fewer than 10 seasons. If multiple, choose the one with the strongest evidence and widest alignment with the sequence (S1 early, S3 near end, S4 mid). Then output only the series title, nothing else.\n\nDOCUMENT ANALYSES:\n" + context_info)
return_result(final_answer)